// The system's prelude (vault designs/policy-language-draft-2026-11-08.md §2): the facts coordd supplies and the
// decisions it asks. Not policy: the facts are filled from the proxy and the price catalog (coordd policy/facts.rs).
Fact model Identified by String
Fact provider Identified by model * String
Fact family Identified by model * String
// the agent harness that runs the model in a session: codex (OpenAI's models), claude (Anthropic's)
Fact harness Identified by model * String
// input price, micro-dollars per million tokens (cpa's resources/model_prices.json); a model without one is not used
Fact price Identified by model * Int

// The reasoning effort a task's calls are made at (paper-research m1405): a level the provider knows (low, medium,
// high), appended to the model model-for chooses for the task, as an agent's MODEL:EFFORT is. A task with none goes out
// with no effort sent (the proxy's default; medium for gpt-5.6-luna).
Fact effort-for Identified by String * String

// How long an owner's step of a call that names a `default` waits for him, in seconds, before it goes on with that
// answer by itself (N-487: the owner's typed words, `look`, 30 s). The shortest instance holds; a call with none waits
// for him as any step does. A project gives it in its own policy: `+lapse-after("look", 30).`
Fact lapse-after Identified by String * Int

// While the owner is writing in the box of the ticket such a step waits on him in (the thread his held post is on), it
// waits on past its `lapse-after`, up to this many seconds since it was owed (E1b, his burst: 15 s, his own rule, the
// owner N-1445 p9; up to 60 s while he types, proto-engine's, with paper-research's yes at N-1446 p40). The
// shortest instance holds; with none, his writing does not hold it.
Fact lapse-at-most Identified by String * Int

// The model of an LLM call, and of an agent coordd makes. An LLM call gives `place` = `call`, `task` (its `task` line),
// `agent` (who it runs for) and `call` (its name). An agent made for a step (`step fresh`, `let agent`) or by
// `coord new` gives `place` = `agent`, `agent` (its name), `call` (the step's call; `coord new` for one made so) and
// `where` (the call's condition on its model, if any; the models that do not meet it are left out, coordd models.rs).
Decision model-for
  Options model
  Requires price(option) >= 0

// Fallback mode (the owner, 20 Nov): the model of an LLM call coordd runs itself when model-for's every option was
// refused for a limit (the gateway's 429, `usage_limit_reached`), asked with the same fields as model-for. Its option is
// the one `fallback(TASK, MODEL)` names for the call's task; a task with none has no fallback, and its call fails as
// before (coordd policy/mod.rs `call_prompt`).
Decision fallback-model
  Options model
  Requires price(option) >= 0
Fact fallback Identified by String * model

// An agent's model is one a harness runs in a session, and coordd starts its agents in Claude Code (roster add).
Only for model-for When call.place == "agent":
  harness(option, "claude")

// A net's session is a harness session (owner m116): its model must be one a harness runs. The call gives
// `place` = `session` for a session's first call.
Only for model-for When call.place == "session":
  harness(option, _)

// The team (coordd supplies these for every norm query, policy/norms.rs): each agent, its role (`coord role`; an agent
// given none is a member), the mail thread a query is about ("none" outside a thread), and the agents the owner wrote to
// in that thread.
Fact agent Identified by String
Fact role Identified by agent * String
Fact thread Identified by String
Fact brought-in Identified by agent * thread

// Teams and model tiers (vault designs/teams-and-tiers-2026-11-10.md §3), supplied for every norm query: each agent's
// model (its effort suffix dropped), its parent (none for the owner's own), a team grant (N agents allowed, U added so
// far) and whether it was added to a team. The proxy's `model` and `family` facts are supplied to the norms too.
Fact runs Identified by agent * model
Fact parent Identified by agent * agent
// BELOW(A, B): A is below B, B's child or further down its tree (from the parents, supplied the same way)
Fact below Identified by agent * agent
Fact granted Identified by agent * Int
Fact used Identified by agent * Int
Fact member Identified by agent

// A decision among agents (`decision NAME(agents: [Agent], ...) -> Agent`, claims.call), supplied when it is asked:
// AMONG(A, I), A the I-th of the agents it is given, from 0 (for `fills`, the I-th text of its step's lists, which need
// not name agents: a text change's names, tickets.eflint); IN-TURN(A) for each agent in a turn now; ABOUT(A) for each
// agent whose work its words are about: a ticket the words name (N-12), or one under it, awaits A's step; WAKEABLE(A)
// below.
Fact among Identified by agent * Int
Fact in-turn Identified by agent
Fact about Identified by agent
// WAKEABLE(A): agent A takes a hand-over now: running, and not ended.
Fact wakeable Identified by agent

// Agents made (item 11; coordd make.rs). MADE(A, BY, FROM, THREAD): agent A was made by
// BY (an agent, or "program" for a program's `let agent`) copying FROM ("none": a fresh one) in THREAD (the top ticket
// of the step BY owed; "none" when it owed none; "t" when it is the thread asked about). SOURCE: the agent a
// `make-agent` copies, or "none". A project that lets agents make agents declares
//   Act make-agent / Actor agent / Recipient agent / Related to source, thread
// (none declared: no agent makes one).
Fact made Identified by String * String * String * String
Fact source Identified by String
